<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21902" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imperturbātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		2. in-perturbatus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>undisturbed</i>, <i>unruffled</i>,
				<i>calm</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imperturbato ore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					562</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">publicis occupationibus quies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 73 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">audio imperturbatus, interritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 9, 13, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui constans est, inperturbatus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 85, 2</span></i>
			; cf. ib. § 3.</div>
